From 496d202f6912a5634b3d7ac401c852ea0cdb50ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snarayana <snarayana@student.ethz.ch>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:03:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(verify): calibrate the noise floor; exact where it
 reproduces, statistical where not

The 1e-6 per-token check is bitwise equality: it fails correct loads
whenever the candidate does not run the reference's kernels on the
reference's shapes. This repo's own Llama-3.1-70B fixtures at TP4 and
TP8 differ by up to 0.155; a fixture from other hardware drifts by
~1e-1 and fails 16/16 (#22); FP4 models fail bitwise. A hand-picked
tolerance would trade those false alarms for missed faults.

`--record --calibrate N` measures the trusted server's own noise: one
repeat of the reference schedule (does it reproduce bitwise?) and N
captures under perturbed load (concurrency, filler traffic, shuffled
order), stored in the reference. `--reference --mode` then decides:

  exact        bitwise; on a mismatch it says whether the drift is
               within the calibrated noise, and still fails
  statistical  per-token drift over s * (1 - p) -- a token's logprob
               noise scales with 1 - p, as the TP4/TP8 fixtures show
               across six decades -- tested by max_z, rms_z and a
               one-sided NLL shift against leave-one-out prediction
               bounds at --alpha, plus margin-aware top-1 and greedy
               checks that explain near-ties instead of failing them
  auto         exact if the calibration proved the schedule reproduces,
               statistical otherwise; legacy for uncalibrated references
  legacy       the original --token-tol/--nll-tol, unchanged

`--calibration-from` adds benign captures from other nodes, restarts or
TP degrees. `--weights` records and compares SGLang's /weights_checker
checksums (>= 0.5.20). Captures move to format 2: full-precision
logprobs, top-2 alternatives per position and greedy step; format-1
references keep working.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
